	)
	(text "CLOCKING - HSE crystal fitted (design review: \"add crystal for USB\").\nX1 = 25 MHz, CL 6 pF, +/-20 ppm, ESR 80 ohm max, 4-pad SMD with the case pads grounded.\nThis is the same part class as X3 on the Nucleo-H723ZG (NDK NX2016SA 25MHz), which is the\nboard this design follows. Load caps C49/C50 = 5.6 pF C0G:\n     CL = (C49 x C50)/(C49 + C50) + Cstray = 2.8 + ~3 = ~5.8 pF, matching the crystal's 6 pF.\nNo series damping resistor: at 25 MHz with 80 ohm ESR the H7 oscillator drive level is within\nST AN2867 limits, and the Nucleo does not fit one either (its SB3/SB4 are only there to switch\nbetween the crystal and the ST-LINK MCO, which this board does not have).\n\nPIN COST OF THE CRYSTAL - PH0/PH1 had to be freed:\n  before:  PH0-OSC_IN (p23) = DIP4      PH1-OSC_OUT (p24) = DIP5\n  after:   PH0/PH1 = X1                 DIP4 -> PF5 (p15)   DIP5 -> PF6 (p18)\nPC14-OSC32_IN (p8) is still USER_EXTI2, so there is NO LSE and no RTC crystal. PC15 (p9) is free,\nso if an LSE is ever needed, move USER_EXTI2 to PE1 (p142, EXTI1 unused) and fit a 32.768 kHz part.\nUSB can now run from the HSE/PLL instead of HSI48 + CRS; HSI48+CRS remains a fallback if X1 is\ndepopulated.\n\nVDDA / VREF+ - the ferrite bead is GONE (design review: \"drop ferrite bead\").\nVDDA (p33) and VREF+ (p32) now tie straight to +3V3, which is what the Nucleo-H723ZG does.\nThe decoupling is unchanged and is what actually matters: C28+C29 (1uF + 100nF) at VDDA and\nC30+C31 (1uF + 100nF) at VREF+. They are NOT interchangeable at layout - each pin needs its\nown pair sitting beside it.\nPDR_ON (p143) tied to +3V3 = internal power-down reset enabled. VBAT (p6) tied to +3V3, no\nbackup battery. VCAP1/VCAP2 each take 2.2uF to GND as the H7 core LDO requires."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 47.24 226.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6e72a872-6b7d-4d79-a1da-1d60491f31a6")
	)
